  "deviations": [
    {
      "actual": "2,854,800 windows",
      "id": "D1",
      "impact": "none; the dropped row carries no training target",
      "planned": "run the encoder over all 2,860,440 sensor windows",
      "topic": "converted corpus is one timestep shorter per episode",
      "why": "2,860,440 counts the raw V10.8 HDF5 corpus. The converted ACT corpus drops each episode's trailing empty action row (proven V5 semantics), giving 71,370 timesteps. Embeddings are generated over the converted corpus, which is what training reads."
    },
    {
      "actual": "episode_horizon=635; raw T_max=627, converted T_max=626",
      "id": "D2",
      "impact": "none; the value is unchanged from the plan",
      "planned": "episode_horizon=635 because verified T_max=627",
      "topic": "episode_horizon justification",
      "why": "627 is the raw HDF5 maximum; the converted maximum is one lower. 635 exceeds both and matches the V5 chunk-100 experiment exactly."
    },
    {
      "actual": "the semantic tree hash is recorded but dropped as an integrity anchor after the encoding pass",
      "id": "D3",
      "impact": "none -- training verifies act_file_sha256 and converted_tree_file_sha256, which are raw-file byte digests and are deterministic",
      "planned": "write conversion and tree-hash manifests",
      "topic": "inherited semantic-hash defect",
      "why": "the V5 converter's _semantic_sha256 hashes numpy object arrays with tobytes(), which serialises pointers rather than string contents; observations/proximity_sensor_names is such a dataset"
    },
    {
      "actual": "the split and evaluation manifests are written as text so their self-hashes validate on reload",
      "id": "D4",
      "impact": "none; both superseded attempts are retained and neither was used",
      "planned": "write create-only manifests",
      "topic": "self-hash collisions with the immutable writer",
      "why": "write_immutable_create_only appends its own payload_sha256, which the split and evaluation loaders then include when recomputing the self-hash, making the manifest permanently unloadable. Caught by loading through the real training loader before training started."
    },
    {
      "actual": "split.source_collection_tree_sha256 is the pre-embedding tree 52391a7eefbdea97b6d09a8c93cea7428a77f2b43bf69a713e1f3b4634ad239e; training verified the post-embedding tree 9565875b415018d35d164b10555d74d98c077c1c24fa7c456df76c2a6a5e05ec",
      "id": "D5",
      "impact": "none. fixed_split_data.verify_dataset cross-checked every split episode against the encoded manifest and matched all 141, and training verified --expect_dataset_tree_sha256 against the post-embedding tree. Not corrected in place because doing so would change split_manifest_sha256 and invalidate the completed runs; both hashes are recorded and each is correct for what it names.",
      "planned": "one split manifest bound to the converted dataset",
      "topic": "the split manifest names the pre-embedding tree hash",
      "why": "the split was built from conversion_manifest.json, whose file hashes predate the embedding pass. The episode identities are identical in both manifests, and the split assignment depends only on attempt_id and cell, never on a file hash."
    }
  ],
